<title>UK: EMI falls after capital reconstructuring.</title>
<headline>EMI falls after capital reconstructuring.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in EMI Group Plc eased on Monday following a capital distribution and share split, dealers said.</p>
<p>EMI shares fell 7-1/4p to 532-1/2p by 0850 GMT in volume of 2,600 shares.</p>
<p>Dealers said shareholders would receive nine new shares and five &quot;B&quot; shares for every five ordinary shares held.  </p>
<p>EMI said the resolution for the reconstruction was passed by shareholders on July 18 and shareholders would be able to redeem their &quot;B&quot; shares free of dealing charges in the period between July 22 and August 19.</p>
<p>However, the decline in EMI's shares was more or less in line with a fall in the UK market overall, dealers noted.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Langlands, London Newsroom +171 542 3496</p>
